## Our Four Audix Gooseneck Table Microphones

Our table microphones are four Audix gooseneck units: two ADX12 and two ADX212. Each one sits on a K&M base with an Audix D-Clip. A gooseneck has a flexible neck, so you can adjust its height and angle toward the speaker's mouth, and it is wired, which means it runs into the mixing console of the sound system rather than working on its own. The same four serve a lectern or a table, so four is the ceiling of what we own for this kind of microphone.

![Two HK Audio speakers on tripods and a panel table with gooseneck microphones, in front of a low stage at a Volvo dealership in Malaga.](https://cdn.malagaeventgear.com/blog/1266/volvo_mice_event_setup-1024x765.webp "Gooseneck microphones on a panel table at a Volvo dealership in Malaga, where we supplied only the audio system: HK Audio speakers on tripods and the microphones.")

We do not publish a technical sheet for them. No pickup pattern, no frequency range, and no claim of an on microphone volume knob, a mute button, Bluetooth, USB or noise cancelling. If one of those matters for your meeting, tell us and we say plainly what we can and cannot offer.

