## Which Package Includes a Table Microphone

Two of our packages include one. The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) at 295 euros ex VAT includes one professional gooseneck microphone, a 3000 lumen projector with a 2x2m screen and sound reinforcement for up to 40 guests. It is built for a boardroom, a private salon or a hotel suite. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) at 490 euros ex VAT includes one gooseneck plus one wireless handheld microphone, a 60 inch LED display and a technician on site for up to 6 hours, for up to 120 guests.

None of our other three packages includes a gooseneck. Neither MICE package includes more than one. If your meeting has several seated speakers, the package is the base and the extra table microphones are added on top by quote.

## How Many Table Microphones a Meeting Needs

We do not apply a fixed ratio such as one microphone per person. The number depends on who speaks, how the table is laid out and how the room sounds. A meeting where one or two people present and the rest listen is a different job from a round table where everyone takes part. Tell us the seating layout and how many people will speak when you ask for a quote, and we propose a setup.

Take a 10 person meeting. Start from the package: one gooseneck in the Basic MICE Pack, plus a wireless handheld in the MICE Pack that can be passed to whoever speaks. Then add table microphones for the seats where people will speak most. We own four, so up to four can come from our own inventory, if they are free on your date. A fifth or more is not in our own inventory: tell us what you need and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one.

## Table Microphone or Wireless Microphone: Which Fits a Meeting?

A table microphone fits speakers who stay seated in one place. A wireless microphone fits someone who moves or hands the microphone on. Compare them by use, not by specification:

| Microphone | Fits best | Keep in mind |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Gooseneck table microphone (Audix ADX12, ADX212) | Seated speakers at a boardroom table, a panel table or a lectern | Wired, so the speaker stays within reach of the stand |
| Wireless handheld (Audix) | Q&A, a speaker who walks, a microphone passed around the room | Someone has to hold it and pass it on |
| Lavalier (AUDIX RAD-360) | A presenter who needs both hands free and a discreet microphone | 2 sets only, a quoted add on outside the packages |
| Headband (AUDIX HT5) | A presenter who moves and gestures | 1 unit only, visible on camera, a quoted add on |

For a presenter who wants both hands free, our [headset and lavalier microphone rental](/blog/headset-lavalier-microphone-rental/) guide covers the two lavalier sets and the headband microphone in detail. One way to mix both kinds is a gooseneck at the table and a wireless handheld for questions, which is exactly how the MICE Pack is built.

## Who Controls the Volume, and Is a Technician Included?

The level of each table microphone is set on the mixing console. Our crew sets it while installing and testing the system before your meeting, adjusting gain and microphone placement for the room. Our [audio system calibration](/blog/audio-system-calibration/) guide explains gain staging in plain terms.

During the meeting, who touches the console depends on the package. The MICE Pack includes a technician on site for up to 6 hours, who operates the sound and the microphones and solves any fault with the sound or the screen. An extra hour is 40 euros. On the Basic MICE Pack a technician is optional at 240 euros per day, and without one the levels set at installation stay as they are, so your own team handles any change at the console. The speaker always runs their own slides.

## Table Microphones for Video Calls and Hybrid Meetings

Our table microphones feed our sound system, so the people in the room hear every speaker. We do not promise that the room mix can be sent into a video call. How a remote participant hears the room depends on how the call is connected, so tell us which laptop and which software you use and we confirm what is possible before you book.

What we supply is the room side: sound, microphones, and a projector with a screen or a 60 inch LED display. You bring your laptop, your conferencing software and your internet connection. Cameras and streaming are not in our own inventory. Speakerphones, conference phones and video conferencing hardware are not either, and for that reason we name no brand or model. Tell us what you need and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one. Our guide to [audio visual rental for corporate meetings](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-corporate-meetings/) covers that split for hybrid meetings.

## How Much Does a Table Microphone Rental Cost?

The cost has three parts. The package comes first: 295 euros ex VAT for the Basic MICE Pack or 490 euros ex VAT for the MICE Pack, with transport and setup included and 21 percent Spanish VAT added on top. The technician comes second: included for up to 6 hours on the MICE Pack, 240 euros per day on the Basic MICE Pack.

Extra table microphones come third. We do not publish a price for one on its own, so we will not guess a figure here. Tell us the meeting and we quote the package and the extra microphones together.

## How to Choose a Conference Table Microphone Rental

Whoever you hire, these five questions are worth asking. Here are our answers:

-   **Who owns the microphones?** Four Audix gooseneck table microphones are ours. Anything beyond them is sourced from suppliers, and we tell you so.
-   **How are they connected?** Wired to the mixing console of the sound system.
-   **Who sets them up and tests them?** Our crew delivers, installs and tests them. We work delivery only, with no self pickup.
-   **Who operates them during the meeting?** A technician, if your package includes one or you add one. Otherwise the levels stay as set.
-   **What is not covered?** Speakerphones, conference phones, video conferencing hardware, cameras and streaming are not in our own inventory.

